              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 320,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 110,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "12 : 6 squashed",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 250,
                "text": "stretch one side → shape changes",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Multiply or divide every term by the same number. Never add.",
          "write": "times, never plus"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Ratios with decimals",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Simplest form means whole numbers, with no common factor.",
          "write": "whole numbers, HCF 1"
        },
        {
          "say": "Simplify 1.2 to 3. Multiply both by 10 to clear the decimal.",
          "write": "1.2 : 3 → 12 : 30"
        },
        {
          "say": "The HCF of 12 and 30 is 6. Divide both by 6.",
          "write": "12 : 30 → 2 : 5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Clear, then cut.",
          "write": "clear, then cut"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Ratios with fractions",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Three quarters to two fifths. The LCM of 4 and 5 is 20.",
          "write": "¾ : ⅖"
        },
        {
          "say": "Multiply both by 20. That gives 15 and 8.",
          "write": "× 20 → 15 : 8"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't just use the denominators. A half to three quarters is not 2 to 4.",
          "write": "✗ ½ : ¾ = 2 : 4"
        },
        {
          "say": "Mixed numbers? Make them improper first.",
          "write": "mixed → improper"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Three terms",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "24 to 36 to 60 compares three amounts.",
          "write": "24 : 36 : 60"
        },
        {
          "say": "The HCF of all three is 12.",
          "write": "HCF = 12"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide every term by 12. That's 2 to 3 to 5.",
          "write": "= 2 : 3 : 5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Finding a missing term",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "4 to 7 equals 10 to x. What happened to the 4?",
          "write": "4 : 7 = 10 : x"
        },
        {
          "say": "4 became 10. The multiplier is 10 divided by 4, which is 2.5.",
          "write": "10 ÷ 4 = 2.5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Do the same to 7. 7 times 2.5 is 17.5.",
          "write": "x = 7 × 2.5 = 17.5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Don't add. 3 to 5 equals x to 20 means times 4, so x is 12.",
          "write": "✗ add 15   ✓ × 4"
        }
      ]
    },
